      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int 2{e}^{3x}{({e}^{3x}+1)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u={e}^{3x}+1.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{3x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\text{d}u=2{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{e}^{3x}{({e}^{3x}+1)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {({e}^{3x}+1)}^{3}\\cdot 2{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{3}\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\int {u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\frac{{u}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{({e}^{3x}+1)}^{4}}{6}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
